{"from": "claim:lk-12-01-yeast-pharisees-hypocrisy", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-16-06-leaven-warning", "note": "Luke defines the yeast as hypocrisy and names only the Pharisees; Matthew names the yeast of the Pharisees and Sadducees."}
{"from": "claim:lk-12-01-yeast-pharisees-hypocrisy", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-08-15-leaven-herod", "note": "Mark's version adds the yeast of Herod; Luke's names hypocrisy."}
{"from": "claim:lk-12-06-sparrows-two-assaria", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-10-29-assarion-sparrows", "note": "Luke prices five sparrows for two assaria; Matthew prices two sparrows for one assarion - the same cheap market custom, different numbers."}
{"from": "claim:lk-12-59-lepton-smallest-coin", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-05-26-quadrans", "note": "Luke's 'last penny' is a lepton; Matthew's parallel saying names a kodrantes (quadrans), which two lepta equal (Mark 12:42)."}
{"from": "artifact:babatha-archive", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-12-13-14-inheritance-arbitration", "grade": "C", "note": "The Babatha archive's papyri (96-134 CE, Mahoza at the Dead Sea) document inheritance of property, property transfers and guardianship in a Jewish family - the documentary world of family inheritance, a generation later and under Roman provincial law."}
{"from": "observation:judea-west-rain-south-heat", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-12-54-56-weather-signs", "grade": "C", "note": "Modern climatology confirms both weather signs the crowds read: rain-bearing systems come from the Mediterranean to the west, and the hot dry sharav blows from the desert south. It confirms the custom of reading these signs, not that the saying was spoken."}
{"from": "artifact:assarion-coin", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-12-06-sparrows-two-assaria", "grade": "C", "note": "The assarion, the lowest-value bronze/copper coin named in the verse, is a documented denomination of the period (the same coin Matthew's sparrow saying uses); the coin is documented, the market price is not. Regraded B to C by reviewer 6: the coin documents the assarion denomination, not the market price of sparrows; the denarius is C everywhere on price claims ('two denarii') and the assarion edge is C in Matthew 10:9, and B must cover the whole claim."}
{"from": "artifact:widows-mite-coin", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-12-59-lepton-smallest-coin", "grade": "B", "note": "The bronze lepton (the 'widow's mite' type of Alexander Jannaeus) is documented as the small coin still circulating in the first century; it confirms the coin Luke names as the 'last penny', not the debtor's imprisonment."}
{"from": "observation:judea-west-rain-south-heat", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:biblehub-pulpit-luke-12-54"}
